 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "Let <span data-math=\"p\">p</span> represent the statement, “Last night it snowed,” and let <span data-math=\"q\">q</span> represent the statement, “Today we will go skiing.” Write the symbolic form of each of the following compound statements:\n",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 496948,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Today we will go skiing, but last night it did not snow.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Today we will go skiing, but last night it did not snow.</p>\n<p>Both “and” and “but” use the conjunction connective.</p>\n<p>The given statements:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"p\"></span>: Last night it snowed.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"q\"></span>: Today we will go skiing.</p>\n<p>Break down the compound statement into its components.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Today we will go skiing,</td>\n<td>but</td>\n<td>not</td>\n<td>last night it snowed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"q\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\" \\wedge \"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\" \\sim \"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"p\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span data-math=\"q \\wedge {\\text{~}}p\"></span></p>\n\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"q \\wedge \\text{~}p\">q \\wedge \\text{~}p</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 496949,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Today we will go skiing if and only if it snowed last night.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"q \\leftrightarrow p\">q \\leftrightarrow p</span>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Today we will go skiing if and only if it snowed last night.</p>\n<p>The given statements:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"p\"></span>: Last night it snowed.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"q\"></span>: Today we will go skiing.</p>\n<p>Break down the compound statement into its components.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Today we will go skiing</td>\n<td>if and only if</td>\n<td>it snowed last night</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"q\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\" \\leftrightarrow \"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"p\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span data-math=\"q\"></span> <span data-math=\" \\leftrightarrow \"></span> <span data-math=\"p\"></span></p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 496950,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Last night is snowed or today we will not go skiing.",
   "answers": [],
